      ⍝ Bugs28 #27 regression: a nested ⎕EC/⎕EA used to strip the
      ⍝ outer ⎕EC/⎕EA of its own result wrapper (and protection)
      ⍝ entirely -- Quad_EC::eval_B()'s clear_safe_execution() reset
      ⍝ the CURRENT frame's safe-execution depth to its parent's,
      ⍝ rather than restoring the value it actually had before this
      ⍝ call, which is wrong whenever that frame was itself already a
      ⍝ safe-execution frame (i.e. itself the B of an enclosing ⎕EC).
      ⍝
      ⎕EC '⎕EC ''1+1'''
 1  0 0   1  0 0  2  

      ⎕EC '⎕EC ''1÷0'' ⋄ 8'
 0  5 4  DOMAIN ERROR 
               1÷0    
               ^^     
 1  0 0  8 

      )SIC
      ⎕EC '⎕EC ''7'' ⋄ ⍳'
 1  0 0  7 
 0  2 2  SYNTAX ERROR+
               ⍳
               ^
         Missing mandatory right argument of function ⍳ (at the right end of the
       statement)

      )SIC
      '8' ⎕EA '⎕EC ''⍳'''
 0  2 2  SYNTAX ERROR+
               ⍳
               ^
         Missing mandatory right argument of function ⍳ (at the right end of the
       statement)

      )SIC

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #95): ⎕EC of a ⍎ that hits an SI-modifying
      ⍝ command ()LOAD, )QLOAD, )CLEAR, )RESET, )SIC) can never actually
      ⍝ let that command run -- ⎕EC's whole point is isolating the
      ⍝ caller from exactly this kind of disruption (a )CLEAR from
      ⍝ inside ⎕EC would destroy the very workspace ⎕EC is running in)
      ⍝ -- so the command used to be silently dropped while still being
      ⍝ reported as if it were a real (if oddly-worded, "Command
      ⍝ Pushed") error. Refused with a real, honestly-worded DOMAIN
      ⍝ ERROR instead, and the workspace is left untouched.
      ⍝
      V←42
      Z←⎕EC '⍎'')CLEAR'''
      V
42

      Z
 0  5 4  DOMAIN ERROR
         the SI-modifying command ')CLEAR' cannot be executed from within ⎕EC/⎕E
      A
       

      )ERASE V Z

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(e)): Quad_EC::eoc() folded )MORE info
      ⍝ into Z3 in two broken ways: (1) err.get_error_line_1() may
      ⍝ already carry a trailing '+' of its own (Error's ctor adds one
      ⍝ at throw time whenever )MORE info exists then, which is exactly
      ⍝ whenever this folding applies), so unconditionally appending a
      ⍝ second one gave e.g. "DOMAIN ERROR++"; (2) multi-line )MORE text
      ⍝ (embedded UNI_LF, e.g. Quad_FIO.cc's "Too few arguments..."
      ⍝ messages) was appended as a single (very wide) PrintBuffer row
      ⍝ instead of one row per real line, so ⎕PW-based output wrapping
      ⍝ later cut it at column boundaries instead of the author's
      ⍝ intended line breaks.
      ⍝
      Z←⎕EC '0J1 2⍸1'
      ⊃Z[3]
DOMAIN ERROR+
      0J1 2⍸1
      ^    ^
A⍸B: A contains items that cannot be compared with each other

      Z←⎕EC '(''%d %d'' 5) ⎕FIO[22] 0'
      ⊃Z[3]
LENGTH ERROR+
      '%d %d' 5 ⎕FIO[22]0
      ^         ^
Too few arguments in argument B of: ⎕FIO.fprintf B
    Only 1 argument(s) were provided in B.
    The format string was: '%d %d'

      )ERASE Z

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(z)): ⎕EC (unlike ⍎) ran B through
      ⍝ ExecuteList::fix() as ordinary APL code even when B is a
      ⍝ )command, so ⎕EC ')CLEAR' mis-parsed ")CLEAR" and gave a bogus
      ⍝ "Unbalanced right parenthesis" instead of either running it (a
      ⍝ non-SI-modifying command) or refusing it the same honest way a
      ⍝ )command reached via ⍎ already does (Bugs28 #95).
      ⍝
      QECA←1
      ⎕EC ')VARS QECA'
 1  0 0   QECA  

      ⎕EC ')CLEAR'
 0  5 4  DOMAIN ERROR
         the SI-modifying command ')CLEAR' cannot be executed from within ⎕EC/⎕E
      A
       

      )ERASE QECA

      ⍝ ==================================

